.TH SDL_HINT_CAMERA_DRIVER 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_CAMERA_DRIVER \- A variable that decides what camera backend to use.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_CAMERA_DRIVER \(dqSDL_CAMERA_DRIVER\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
By default, SDL will try all available camera backends in a reasonable order until it finds one that can work, but this hint allows the app or user to force a specific target, such as \(dqdirectshow\(dq if, say, you are on Windows Media Foundations but want to try DirectShow instead\[char46]
.PP
The default value is unset, in which case SDL will try to figure out the best camera backend on your behalf\[char46] This hint needs to be set before
.BR SDL_Init ()
is called to be useful\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

